{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgLRrVteHcgxKCiemJDrp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The fix is in pull request #832 (merge commit `6a5b489`), which made `calcWeightForHeightZscore` convert the height with `Number()` before using it. Falkon links the PR to O3-6048 by ticket pattern, and its body says the old code called `height.toFixed(1)` directly on the raw value, which throws when the value is a string.\n\n**Evidence, best first:**\n\n1. **The fixed helper** (`openmrs-esm-form-engine-lib/src/utils/common-expression-helpers.ts`, lines 493–521). Line 494 converts with `Number(height)`. Line 495 uses that converted value in the missing-value guard, so `\"\"` and `\"abc\"` become `NaN` or `0` and return `null`. Lines 509–513 apply the 45–110 cm range check and the `toFixed(1)` rounding to the converted `numericHeight`, not the raw input. The JSDoc at line 489 notes that numeric strings are accepted.\n\n2. **New string-height tests** (`openmrs-esm-form-engine-lib/src/utils/common-expression-helpers.test.ts`, lines 605–621). These cover string heights such as `'65.2'` and `'80'`, out-of-range `'44.9'` and `'110.1'`, and invalid `'0'`, `''` and `'abc'`, all expected to return `null` where invalid.\n\n3. **Pull request #832**, \"(fix) O3-6048: Accept numeric string height in calcWeightForHeightZscore\". It is merged, changes two files (6 lines added and 5 removed in the helper, 18 added in the test), and was approved by denniskigen. The PR body says the new string-height cases fail on main with `height.toFixed is not a function` and pass with the change. I did not run the tests myself.\n\n4. **Merge commit `6a5b489`**, which is the change on main. The Greptile review refers to head commit `fe485d7` as the last reviewed commit.\n\n5. **Ticket O3-6048**. The PR links it, along with related tickets O3-6025 and O3-6046.\n\nOther notes:\n- The string-height call paths come from `defaultValue` or `rendering: \"text\"`, per the PR body. I did not trace the form-engine code that passes those values in.\n- The helper's registration in `openmrs-esm-form-engine-lib/src/utils/zscore-service.ts` (line 27) was not changed by the fix. It only maps the helper to its reference tables.\n- I did not read the pre-fix version of the helper directly. The \"before\" behavior comes from the PR description.\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-form-engine-lib/src/utils/common-expression-helpers.ts\", \"startLine\": 493, \"endLine\": 521},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-form-engine-lib/src/utils/common-expression-helpers.test.ts\", \"startLine\": 605, \"endLine\": 621},\n  {\"repo\": \"openmrs-esm-form-engine-lib\", \"pr\": 832},\n  {\"repo\": \"openmrs-esm-form-engine-lib\", \"commit\": \"6a5b489b47c58f526f9988624c0bf349ec5b75ad\"},\n  {\"ticket\": \"O3-6048\"}\n]\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2283,"cache_read_input_tokens":23828,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2283},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"74398faf-1554-4108-a837-faa586da9445","uuid":"e66e5fc7-13c0-40be-9f0b-ada0e1fc90a8","timestamp":"2026-10-24T04:27:15.790Z","request_id":"req_011CgLRrVbHRafVwMNEB9e5P"}
